@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Map";
}
<h1>Map</h1>
<p class="muted">Pyro, Stanton and Nyx from above: everybody playing where his quantum jumps put him, and the objectives of the missions going on. In quantum a
  player moves along his route at the speed of his drive (crafted as it is, from his fleet). The log says when he picks a destination and when he arrives,
  not when the jump starts, so on the way it is an estimate; the arrival puts him right. The Hauling Planner's pickups, deliveries and hand-ins place a
  member of the party too, when they are newer. The map opens on the system where most players are.</p>
<div class="maptool">
  <div class="mapbox">
    <div class="systabs" id="systems" role="tablist" aria-label="Star system"></div>
    <div id="map"></div>
    <p class="hint">Positions: the <a href="https://api.star-citizen.wiki" rel="noopener">Star Citizen Wiki API</a>. A moon, a city or a station close
      to a planet is drawn at the planet (point at it for what is there).</p>
    <h2>Active missions</h2>
    <div id="missions"><p class="muted">Loading…</p></div>
    <p class="hint">Every mission going on, with who has it, how many of its objectives are still open, and what the <a href="/missions">Mission Library</a> says about it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mapside">
    <h2>Players</h2>
    <div id="players"><p class="muted">Loading…</p></div>
    <h2>Objectives</h2>
    <div id="objectives"></div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint" id="mapState"></p>
@if (User.IsInRole(Roles.Admin))
{
  <p class="hint"><a href="/admin/places">Map places</a>: say what a destination the map does not know is, rename a place, add one.</p>
}
<script src="~/systemmap.js" asp-append-version="true" defer></script>
<script src="~/map.js" asp-append-version="true" defer></script>
